<title>USA: TABLE-Summit Holding net rises in June qtr.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Summit Holding net rises in June qtr.</headline>
<dateline>LAKELAND, Fla. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Selected Financial Data</p>
<p>				     (unaudited)</p>
<p>			(in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						     Three months ended</p>
<p>							   June 30,</p>
<p>							1997	     1996</p>
<p>  Revenue				     $ 17,225	 $ 37,109</p>
<p> Net income					2,539	    1,274</p>
<p> Earnings per share			     0.46		 --</p>
<p> Weighted average no. shares		 5,400		 --</p>
<p> Outstanding shares			    5,791</p>
<p>Net results for the quarter include an after-tax gain  of $500,000, or $0.10 per share, from net realized investment gains.</p>
<p>Revenues for the quarter decreased because the company entered into a quota share reinsurance agreement on April 1, which resulted in a loss of 75 percent of the net premiums written.</p>
<p>The company went public in May, 1997.</p>
<p>Full name is Summit Holding Southeast Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
